            <ArticleTitle>Intranasal administration of midazolam to a severely burned child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>307-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This report describes the use of intranasally administered midazolam for sedation in a critically ill burned paediatric patient without venous access. Placement of a central venous catheter was successfully carried out following sedation by this method.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
